ai/DELL: llm 85 (HIGH) — Dell's $95B non-cancelable AI server backlog, raised FY27 guidance, and leading branded server share make it a prime, estimate-upgrade-driven AI infrastructure winner despite thin hardware margins.
ai/MDB: llm 68 (MEDIUM) — MongoDB's Atlas consumption and early AI/Voyage monetization are compounding with raised guidance and rising estimates, but leadership chaos and Postgres-driven share risk temper conviction.
ai/MU: llm 92 (HIGH) — Micron is the structural picks-and-shovels winner of the AI memory supercycle, with sold-out HBM4 supply, record margins, and accelerating estimate revisions that still appear underpriced at ~7x forward earnings.
grid/BE: llm 74 (MEDIUM) — Bloom is the clearest picks-and-shovels play on AI-driven grid bottlenecks with accelerating bookings and guidance raises, but customer concentration, negative operating cash flow, and backlog-accounting scrutiny cap conviction despite strong estimate momentum.
grid/ATKR: llm 0 (LOW) — ATKR was acquired by Prysmian for $95.00/share cash and completed delisting from the NYSE on October 19, 2026, so it no longer exists as an investable public equity despite genuine grid/data-center tailwinds pre-deal.
grid/NVT: llm 83 (HIGH) — nVent is an early-stage share-gainer in AI-driven data center electrification with accelerating product launches, raised guidance every quarter, and broad-based analyst upgrades, offset only by hyperscaler customer concentration risk.
robotics/ZBRA: llm 71 (MEDIUM) — Zebra is a high-momentum automation enabler (machine vision, RFID, AI) with real pricing power and accelerating estimates, but it divested its actual robotics (AMR) business in 2026, diluting pure robotics-theme exposure.
robotics/CGNX: llm 68 (MEDIUM) — Cognex is riding a genuine AI-vision product cycle and diversifying into robotic perception via RealSense, but stretched valuation, revenue misses, and insider selling temper near-term conviction.
robotics/EMR: llm 60 (MEDIUM) — Emerson is a high-quality process-automation compounder riding AI/software (AspenTech) and energy-infrastructure capex, but it's an indirect robotics-theme play with premium valuation and mixed Street sentiment.
defense/RDW: llm 54 (MEDIUM) — Redwire's revenue and backlog are inflecting on real multi-domain defense/space contract wins, but heavy dilution, unresolved governance/control issues, and newly cautious sell-side coverage cap conviction until profitability and competitive differentiation are proven.
defense/CACI: llm 74 (HIGH) — Record $4.8B awards, double-digit funded-backlog growth, and back-to-back guidance raises around new AI/counter-UAS/space platforms (Apollo, SkyValor, ARKA) signal a product cycle inflecting upward with broad estimate-revision support.
defense/HEI: llm 74 (HIGH) — HEICO is compounding through a still-early aftermarket replacement cycle while its defense/space electronics segment is inflecting sharply, backed by five straight beats and a strong proprietary-parts moat, though rich valuation caps near-term upside.
health/NTRA: llm 84 (HIGH) — Natera's MRD franchise is compounding through regulatory/guideline catalysts and expanding TAM, backed by unusually strong and broad-based analyst estimate upgrades, despite litigation and insider-selling overhangs.
health/LLY: llm 88 (HIGH) — Lilly's GLP-1 franchise is entering a second growth wave via orforglipron and expanding indications, with broad-based analyst upgrades confirming estimate momentum even as the stock hits new highs.
health/GH: llm 83 (HIGH) — Guardant is riding a genuine platform inflection as Shield's payer-coverage wall (UnitedHealth, Carelon, EviCore, ACS guidelines) comes down just as oncology volumes keep accelerating, driving broad upward estimate revisions despite real dilution and cash-burn risk.
outlier/PLTR: llm 82 (HIGH) — Palantir's AIP-driven commercial acceleration and entrenched government moat are expanding TAM and driving broad upward estimate revisions, but a near-300x P/E and heavy insider selling/SBC dilution leave zero margin for execution missteps.
outlier/HOOD: llm 74 (MEDIUM) — Robinhood is layering multiple new product cycles (prediction markets, tokenization, agentic trading) onto a still-growing core brokerage with clear market-share gains, but heavy insider selling and dilution risk cap conviction ahead of the Oct 27 print.
outlier/GEV: llm 64 (MEDIUM) — GEV's gas-turbine and grid-equipment backlog is sold out through 2031 on AI-driven power demand with real pricing power, but Wind losses and recent EPS misses are driving near-term estimate cuts despite raised revenue guidance.
